        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.011,
          "end": 4.5,
          "en": "-: In the last lecture, we improved the user experience",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.5,
          "end": 8.283,
          "en": "by taking advantage of the form state handled by Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.283,
          "end": 10.308,
          "en": "Now, let's improve this even more",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.308,
          "end": 12.788,
          "en": "and let's say we want to output some help text",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.788,
          "end": 15.044,
          "en": "below this input to assist",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.044,
          "end": 17.941,
          "en": "if there is an invalid value in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.941,
          "end": 20.339,
          "en": "Now we can use a bootstrap class here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.339,
          "end": 24.15,
          "en": "help-block to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.15,
          "end": 26.46,
          "en": "that this has the appropriate styling.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.46,
          "end": 29.64,
          "en": "And then we could say, Please enter a valid email.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.64,
          "end": 32.7,
          "en": "We only want to show this if a valid, excuse me",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.7,
          "end": 34.89,
          "en": "if an invalid value has been entered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 34.89,
          "end": 38.212,
          "en": "into the control associated with this input though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.212,
          "end": 40.2,
          "en": "Well, a quick and easy way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 40.2,
          "end": 43.11,
          "en": "of getting access to the control created",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 43.11,
          "end": 47.013,
          "en": "by Angler automatically as we added ngModel to the input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 47.013,
          "end": 51.829,
          "en": "is by adding a local reference to this input element here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 51.829,
          "end": 54.337,
          "en": "For example, email, any name you like",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 54.337,
          "end": 57.464,
          "en": "and associating this now, not with NG form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 57.464,
          "end": 62.22,
          "en": "as we did for the overall form, but with ngModel.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.22,
          "end": 65.869,
          "en": "So just like the form directive automatically added",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 65.869,
          "end": 68.797,
          "en": "by Angler when it detects a form element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 68.797,
          "end": 72.819,
          "en": "The ngModel directive here also kind of exposes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 72.819,
          "end": 76.68,
          "en": "some additional information about the control it creates",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 76.68,
          "end": 81.64699999999999,
          "en": "for us on the overarching form by accessing ngModel.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 81.64699999999999,
          "end": 85.02,
          "en": "So with this, we could simply check or say",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 85.02,
          "end": 90.02,
          "en": "that we want to attach this span here if email is not valid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 91.89,
          "end": 94.02799999999999,
          "en": "So add exclamation mark at the beginning.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 94.02799999999999,
          "end": 99.02799999999999,
          "en": "Now if this, if this reloads, you'll see that help text.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 99.137,
          "end": 101.78999999999999,
          "en": "And of course you can improve this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 101.78999999999999,
          "end": 103.27600000000001,
          "en": "by also chaining another condition.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 103.27600000000001,
          "end": 105.22800000000001,
          "en": "That email should have been touched to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 105.22800000000001,
          "end": 107.77199999999999,
          "en": "give the user a chance of changing it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 107.77199999999999,
          "end": 109.53,
          "en": "So now you don't see the warning",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 109.53,
          "end": 111.72,
          "en": "but if you click in there and click out of there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 111.72,
          "end": 113.393,
          "en": "and it is invalid, you see that warning.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 113.393,
          "end": 117.555,
          "en": "And if you now enter a valid data, it disappears.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 117.555,
          "end": 119.02000000000001,
          "en": "So this is another way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 119.02000000000001,
          "end": 122.444,
          "en": "of taking advantage of the state managed by Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 122.444,
          "end": 125.67,
          "en": "but this also shows you how you can get a quick",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 125.67,
          "end": 127.897,
          "en": "and easy access to control added by Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 127.897,
          "end": 131.031,
          "en": "And with that, you should have tools to really",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 131.031,
          "end": 133.558,
          "en": "provide a pleasant user experience",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 133.558,
          "end": 136.5,
          "en": "showing the right errors, the right warnings",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 136.5,
